    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29126" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĭnervālis</span></b> , e,
			adj.
		Minerva, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Minerva</i>
			(to learning, good sense, etc.), <i>Minervan</i>
			(post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">artes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Spect. 11 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">munus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. ad Ephes. 6, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">MAGISTER,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 2421</span></i>
			.— In <i>plur. subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĭnervālĭa</span></b> ,
				ĭum, n., <i>festivities in honor of Minerva</i>, Sergius, p. 1846
